  "intro": "A definite integral of a rate gives the net change in the quantity: $\\int_a^b r(t)\\,dt=Q(b)-Q(a)$. For motion, $\\int_a^b v(t)\\,dt$ is displacement (net change in position), while $\\int_a^b |v(t)|\\,dt$ is total distance traveled. More generally, integrating a flow rate gives total accumulated amount, and adding it to a starting value gives the ending value.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "An object has velocity $v(t)=3t^2$ m/s. Find the displacement from $t=0$ to $t=2$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Displacement is $\\int_0^2 v(t)\\,dt=\\int_0^2 3t^2\\,dt$.",
          "Antiderivative $t^3$: $\\left[t^3\\right]_0^2=8-0$.",
          "So the displacement is $8$ meters."
        ],
        "answer": "$8$ m"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Water flows into a tank at $r(t)=4t$ liters/min. How much enters during the first $5$ minutes?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Total volume is $\\int_0^5 4t\\,dt$.",
          "Antiderivative $2t^2$: $\\left[2t^2\\right]_0^5=50$.",
          "So $50$ liters flow in."
        ],
        "answer": "$50$ liters"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "A particle has velocity $v(t)=t-3$ on $[0,5]$. Find displacement and total distance.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Displacement: $\\int_0^5 (t-3)\\,dt=\\left[\\frac{t^2}{2}-3t\\right]_0^5=\\frac{25}{2}-15=-\\frac{5}{2}$.",
          "Distance needs $|v|$: $v<0$ on $[0,3)$, $v>0$ on $(3,5]$.",
          "$\\int_0^3 (3-t)\\,dt=\\frac{9}{2}$ and $\\int_3^5 (t-3)\\,dt=2$.",
          "Total distance $=\\frac{9}{2}+2=\\frac{13}{2}$."
        ],
        "answer": "Displacement $-\\dfrac{5}{2}$ m; total distance $\\dfrac{13}{2}$ m."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "If $v(t)=2t$, find the displacement on $[0,3]$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$\\int_0^3 2t\\,dt=[t^2]_0^3=9$."
        ],
        "answer": "$9$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "A population grows at $P'(t)=100e^{0.1t}$ per year. Net change over the first $10$ years?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$\\int_0^{10}100e^{0.1t}\\,dt=1000(e^1-1)\\approx 1718$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\approx 1718$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 6,
      "prompt": "A car starts at position $s(0)=5$ with $v(t)=6t$. Find $s(2)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$s(2)=s(0)+\\int_0^2 6t\\,dt=5+[3t^2]_0^2=5+12=17$."
        ],
        "answer": "$s(2)=17$"
      }
    }
  ]
